x86_64-linux  The C1 forms, and nothing else: every C2 name agrees with clang. clang emits only the base-object C2 form of a constructor defined *inside* its class on this target, where cxx1 emits the complete-object C1 beside it - the fact move-constructor.nonames and implicit-move.nonames already record. x86_64-windows and arm64-darwin agree name for name; the access rule this case is about changes no name.
